"""State income tax and state payroll deductions on wages for the take-home pay calculator (/tools/take-home-pay/ and one page per state).

Asked for by the plan of 18 Nov 2026 ("rates only from official sources, each checked by a test, nothing published before that"). A state is here
only when its rates and deductions were read on its own government site or statute on 19 Nov 2026 and the ordinary salary needs no rule we cannot
work out. WAITING lists the others: their figures could not all be read on an official page, or they need a rule still to be built (recapture,
a deduction that shrinks with income, a tax on top of a county tax).

b: brackets of taxable income [upper limit, rate], None for the top. d: standard deduction. e: personal exemption. c: credit taken off the tax.
base "wages": salary less pre-tax contributions; "fed": federal taxable income. pay: [name, rate, wage cap, yearly maximum].

Run `python3 state_tax.py` to check the figures against sums worked out by hand.
"""
